#   P1.2 encode   0.2 to 0.6 against 43 to 45. Between 0.4 and 1.4 percent.
#   P1.1 encode   within +-0.2 against 30. Note hazard 1: four elements.
#   P1.1, P1.2    decode: the FFI arm is FASTER than core-native here and was SLOWER in the
#                 bench binary. Both differences are inside the spread. No per-element
#                 interface cost should be quoted for these two rows in either direction --
#                 which is a correction to the published table, but not the one the
#                 objection predicted.
